requirements/rest-job-view-attachment.yaml:1:title: '[JENKINS-74795] Job created via REST API attaches to default view'
requirements/rest-job-view-attachment.yaml:5:  A Jenkins administrator creating a job through the REST API expects that operation to create the item and leave view membership unchanged unless they explicitly add it to a view, but REST-based creation can incorrectly attach the new job to the default view.
requirements/rest-job-view-attachment.yaml:10:  Creating an item through the standard `createItem` endpoint should behave like a normal item-creation operation, not like an implicit “add to current view” action. A newly created job should exist in Jenkins, but the default view should not be populated as a side effect of that REST call.
requirements/rest-job-view-attachment.yaml:15:  REST-created jobs are available after creation, the default view stays unchanged unless explicitly edited, and the scenario covered by `testCreateItemDoesNotPopulateDefaultView` succeeds without requiring any special client workaround.
requirements/rest-view-lts-backport.yaml:10:  The backported LTS behavior should preserve the REST `createItem` contract so a newly created job is not silently attached to the default view, and the supporting class-loader utility should continue to resolve its caller correctly by retaining a class reference when discovering it. The item-creation endpoint should still be handled as a proper POST operation.
requirements/rest-view-lts-backport.yaml:15:  REST-created jobs remain outside the default view unless explicitly added, POST-based item creation continues to work through the backported endpoint handling, and caller discovery via `SetContextClassLoader` keeps working on the supported runtime without additional caller-side changes.
